# Every change requires review from the maintainer.
#
# Combined with the "main" ruleset's require_code_owner_review, this makes
# @shreyansh-sawarn a mandatory reviewer on all contributor pull requests.
#
# GitHub never requests review from a PR's own author, so this does not block
# the maintainer's own PRs — those are covered by the admin bypass, which is
# scoped to pull requests only and cannot be used to push to main directly.
* @shreyansh-sawarn

# The analysis engine decides whether someone's failing build is their fault.
# A wrong verdict here is worse than no tool at all, so these paths are called
# out explicitly to make review of them deliberate rather than incidental.
/src/core/flake.ts @shreyansh-sawarn
/src/action/ @shreyansh-sawarn

# The committed action bundle is executable code that runs in users' CI.
# Treat any change to it as security-relevant.
/action-dist/ @shreyansh-sawarn
